Bubble Sort has a worst-case and average time complexity of O(n^2), where n is the number of items being sorted. Quick Sort typically has an average time complexity of O(n log n) but in the worst case, can degrade to O(n^2). Given this information, we will first implement Bubble Sort and Quick Sort and then run tests on a large dataset.

